-- title:
--   Fixed ring of Fr² is free of rank two
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime. Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative domain of characteristic $0$ that is a discrete valuation ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$ be irreducible, assume $\mathcal O$ is complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, that the quotient $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and that $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$; let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic $0$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $\mathrm{Onr}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra which is a domain of characteristic $0$, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $\mathrm{Onr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every $x \in \mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $\mathrm{Onr}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^r \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$. Write $\mathcal O_2$ for the equalizer of $\mathrm{Fr} \circ \mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity, i.e. the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of elements fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^2$. Then: $\mathcal O_2$ is a free $\mathcal O$-module of rank $2$; $\mathcal O_2$ is stable under $\mathrm{Fr}$; an element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ is fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}$ exactly when it lies in the image of $\mathcal O$; and $\mathcal O_2$ modulo the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ has exactly $r^2$ elements.
--
--   This is the axiomatic form of the statement that inside the completed maximal unramified extension $W(\bar{\mathbb F}_r)$ of $\mathcal O = \mathbb Z_r$ the ring of $\mathrm{Fr}^2$-fixed points is the unramified quadratic extension $W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$, free of rank two over $\mathcal O$ with residue ring of order $r^2$, while the $\mathrm{Fr}$-fixed points are $\mathcal O$ itself. It is used in the construction of the Mumford-type towers and of the twisted descent data entering the Čerednik–Drinfel'd description, in particular by [`CerednikDrinfeld.UnramQuad.bijective_lift_prod_equalizer_frobenius_sq_tensor`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.UnramQuad.bijective_lift_prod_equalizer_frobenius_sq_tensor), [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordTower.exists_twistedTower`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordTower.exists_twistedTower) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordTower.nonempty_nrPresentation`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordTower.nonempty_nrPresentation).
